    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i was reading about box breathing (like the 4-4-4-4 thing) and was wondering what it actually does to the body? like how does that specific rhythm affect my nervous system or cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, with its equal inhale, hold, exhale, and pause, directly influences your autonomic nervous system. This slow, rhythmic breathing stimulates the vagus nerve, which is a key part of the parasympathetic nervous system—your body's \"rest and digest\" mode. By activating this system, it signals to your body to slow down, helping to reduce the physiological stress response and thereby lowering elevated levels of cortisol. In essence, it nudges your system out of fight-or-flight.",
      "source": "target",
