    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so it's basically just about the vagus nerve then? is there any kind of \"energy\" shift or anything like that when you do it properly, or is it purely just a mechanical/biological thing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the mechanism is strongly biological, the perceived shift is a direct result of that biological regulation. By calming the sympathetic nervous system's overdrive, you shift your mental state from heightened anxiety to one of grounded focus. This isn't just a mechanical trick; the altered state of your nervous system translates into a subjective feeling of reduced stress and increased calm energy. Therefore, the physiological calming creates the experiential shift in your energy.",
      "source": "target",
