    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. do you think there's a limit to how much it helps? like, if someone is in a really chaotic or high-stress environment, is there a point where the body just refuses to respond to the breathing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is possible that severe, acute trauma or extreme physiological stress can make breathing exercises less immediately effective. When the nervous system is in a state of profound dysregulation, responses can become \"stuck\" in sympathetic overdrive. In such moments, while gentle breathing can still offer small benefits, it may not rapidly override the body's intense survival alarms. For very high-stress situations, deep professional support alongside mindful breathing is often necessary.",
      "source": "target",
